cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pf-tea: an open techno-economic model for precision-fermented food proteins"
message: "If you use this model or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Moreno Casares"
    given-names: "Pablo Antonio"
version: "0.4.1"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PabloAMC/precision-fermentation-tea"
keywords:
  - precision fermentation
  - techno-economic analysis
  - beta-lactoglobulin
  - ovalbumin
  - lactoferrin
  - alpha-lactalbumin
  - ovomucoid
  - beta-casein
  - serum albumin
  - Komagataella phaffii
  - bioprocess engineering
abstract: >-
  A public-data-only techno-economic model of food proteins made by precision fermentation,
  following Humbird's (2021) method: element- and electron-balanced stoichiometry, an
  oxygen-transfer-limited fed-batch fermenter, a downstream train and a capital estimate
  anchored to the market price of baker's yeast. Every parameter carries a source and an
  evidence grade. Prepared with an AI assistant and audited by independent AI reviewers;
  not yet peer-reviewed.
